      "content": "I see. So you're essentially saying that the \"sophistication\" of a trend is tied to how much it avoids those \"urban\" or \"struggle\" narratives? \n\nFollow up then: if a brand wanted to tap into that \"street\" energy for a casual line, would it be better to use the AAVE slang or stick to the musical rhythms? Or do those both just inherently lower the brand's perceived status because of the demographics they represent?",
